From 96103537f46c180a12768761c0b06373f4088249 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Five (Xer)" <admin@fivepb.me>
Date: Wed, 23 Jun 2021 23:10:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Rework information forwarding

Enable Bungeeguard and Velocity/Modern forwarding modes natively.

Modern forwarding transports the player's identity to the backend in a
login plugin message on velocity:player_info, authenticated with an
HMAC-SHA256 tag over a shared secret, rather than smuggling it through the
handshake host as the legacy scheme does. The payload version is negotiated
against the backend's request, the client's protocol version and whether the
player presented a key, so 1.19 and 1.19.1 clients get their key block
forwarded and 1.19.3+ clients get the session key model.

forwarding_mode in waterfall.yml selects the mode. It defaults to whatever
ip_forward implies, so existing configurations keep working untouched. The
secret is read from VELOCITY_FORWARDING_SECRET or forwarding_secret_file as
well as the config, so it can be shared with a Velocity proxy, and is
generated on first start when a mode needs one and none is configured.

Clients below 1.13 are refused up front, as they cannot carry login plugin
messages.

Based on PaperMC/Waterfall#663 by Five (Xer). The BungeeGuard plugin
detection warning from the original patch is omitted.

Co-authored-by: Shane Freeder <theboyetronic@gmail.com>

